"code":"BinaryFloatingPoint"},{"text":" types. All of the Swift standard library’s floating-point types, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float80","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryFloatingPoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and therefore work with this format style.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" includes two nested types, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","type":"reference"},{"text":", for working with percentages and currencies, respectively. Each format style includes a configuration that determines how it represents numeric values, for things like grouping, displaying signs, and variant presentations like scientific notation. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","type":"reference"},{"text":" include a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/NumberFormatStyleConfiguration","type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","type":"reference"},{"text":" includes a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/CurrencyFormatStyleConfiguration","type":"reference"},{"text":". You can customize numeric formatting for a style by adjusting its backing configuration. The system automatically caches unique configurations of a format style to enhance performance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Foundation provides another format style type, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/IntegerFormatStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for working with numbers that conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":" For Foundation’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type, use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal\/FormatStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Formatting-floating-point-values","text":"Formatting floating-point values","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryFloatingPoint.formatted()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method to create a string representation of a floating-point value using the default ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" configuration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let formattedDefault = 12345.67.formatted()","\/\/ formattedDefault is \"12,345.67\" in the en_US locale.","\/\/ Other locales may use different separator and grouping behavior."],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can specify a format style by providing an argument to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryFloatingPoint.formatted(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The following example shows the number ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represented in each of the available styles, in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" locale:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let number = 0.1","","let formattedNumber = number.formatted(.number)","\/\/ formattedNumber is \"0.1\".","","let formattedPercent = number.formatted(.percent)","\/\/ formattedPercent is \"10%\".","","let formattedCurrency = number.formatted(.currency(code: \"USD\"))","\/\/ formattedCurrency is \"$0.10\"."],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each style provides methods for updating its numeric configuration, including the number of significant digits, grouping length, and more. You can specify a numeric configuration by calling as many of these methods as you need in any order you choose. The following example shows the same number with default and custom configurations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let exampleNumber = 123456.78","","let defaultFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(.number)","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123 456,78\" for the \"fr_FR\" locale.","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123,456.78\" for the \"en_US\" locale.","","let customFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(",".number",".grouping(.never)",".sign(strategy: .always()))","\/\/ customFormatting is \"+123456.78\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Creating-a-floating-point-format-style-instance","text":"Creating a floating-point format style instance","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The previous examples use static factory methods like ","type":"text"},{"code":"FormatStyle.number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to create format styles within the call to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryFloatingPoint\/formatted(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. You can also create a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" instance and use it to repeatedly format different values, with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/format(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let percentFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Percent()","","percentFormatStyle.format(0.5) \/\/ \"50%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(0.855) \/\/ \"85.5%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(1.0) \/\/ \"100%\"",""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Parsing-floating-point-values","text":"Parsing floating-point values","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" to parse strings into floating-point values. You can define the format style within the type’s initializer or pass in a format style created outside the function, as shown here:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let price = try? Double(\"$3,500.63\",","format: .currency(code: \"USD\")) \/\/ 3500.63","","let priceFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Currency(code: \"USD\")","let salePrice = try? Double(\"$731.67\",","format: priceFormatStyle) \/\/ 731.67"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Matching-regular-expressions","text":"Matching regular expressions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Along with parsing numeric values in strings, you can use theSwift regular expression domain-specific language to match and capture numeric substrings. The following example defines a percentage format style to match a percentage value using ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" numeric conventions. The rest of the regular expression ignores any characters prior to a ","type":"text"},{"code":"\": \"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sequence that precedes the percentage substring.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import RegexBuilder","let source = \"Percentage complete: 55.1%\"","let matcher = Regex {","OneOrMore(.any)","\": \"","Capture {","One(.localizedDoublePercentage(locale: Locale(identifier: \"en_US\")))","}","}","let match = source.firstMatch(of: matcher)","let localizedPercentage = match?.1","print(\"\\(localizedPercentage!)\") \/\/ 0.551"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"}],"title":"FloatingPointFormatStyle","modules":[{"name":"FoundationInternationalization"}],"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"12.0","beta":false,"name":"macOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false,"name":"tvOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false}],"navigatorT